WEBVTT

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.440
Oh, yeah! Whoo!

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.600
Yep! All right! Got it!

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.160
"First one to California
gets Dinoco all to himself."

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.880
Oh, we'll see
who gets there first, Chick.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.040
Huh?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.480
- Hey, kid! Congrats on the tie.
- I don't want to talk about it.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.400
Let's go, Mack. Saddle up.
What'd you do with my trailer?

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.640
- I parked it at your sponsor's tent.
- What?

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.720
Gotta make your personal appearance.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.360
No. No! No, no, no, no!

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.880
Yes, yes, yes!
Lightning McQueen here.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.600
And I use Rust-eze Medicated
Bumper Ointment, new rear end formula!

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.360
Nothing soothes a rusty bumper
like Rust-eze.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.200
Wow! Look at that shine!

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.000
Use Rust-eze and you too
can look like me!

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.320
Ka-chow!

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.000
[both laughing]

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.640
I met this car from Swampscott.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.760
He was so rusty
he didn't even cast a shadow.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.680
- You could see his dirty undercarriage.
- [crowd laughs]

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.000
[groaning] I hate rusty cars.
This is not good for my image.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.480
They did give you your big break.
Besides, it's in your contract.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.440
Oh, will you stop, please?
Just go get hooked up.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.480
- Winter is a grand old time.
- Of this there are no ifs or buts.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.960
[male 1] But remember,
all that salt and grime...

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.040
Can rust your bolts and freeze your...

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.040
Hey, look! There he is!

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.080
Our almost champ!

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.800
[male 1] Get your rear end in here.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.920
Lightning McQueen,
you are wicked fast!

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.160
- That race was a pisser!
- You were booking!

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.280
- Give me a little room.
- You're my hero!

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.200
Yes, I know. [chuckles]

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.840
"Fred." Fred, thank you.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.520
He knows my name.
He knows my name!

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.560
Looking good, Freddie!

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.040
Thanks to you, Lightning,
we had a banner year!

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.680
We might clear enough
to buy you some headlights.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.760
You saying he doesn't have headlights?

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.160
That's what I'm telling ya.
They're stickers!

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.240
Well, you know,
racecars don't need headlights,

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.320
because the track is always lit.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.560
Yeah, well, so is my brother,
but he still needs headlights.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.320
[laughing]

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.400
[forced laughter]

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.240
- Ladies and gentlemen,
- [both] Lightning McQueen!

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.160
[crickets chirping]

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.160
Free Bird!

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.560
You know, the Rust-eze Medicated
Bumper Ointment team

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.480
ran a great race today.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.240
And remember, with a little Rust-eze...

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.520
[whispering] And an insane
amount of luck,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.080
...you too, can look like me.
Ka-chow.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.240
- Hey, kid.
- We love ya.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.760
And we're looking forward
to another great year.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.080
Just like this year!

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.960
Not on your life.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.760
- Don't drive like my brother!
- Yeah, don't drive like my brother!

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.880
California, here we come!

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.600
Dinoco, here we come!

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.680
[♪ Rascal Flatts: Life is a Highway]

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.800
[birds chirping]

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.720
[phone ringing]

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:41.400
[moaning] Oh... oh ... uh,
I needed this. Hello?

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.040
[male] Is this Lightning McQueen,
the world's fastest racing machine?

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.240
Is this Harv,
the world's greatest agent?

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.080
And it is such an honor
to be your agent

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.200
that it almost hurts me to take
ten percent of your winnings.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.360
Merchandising. And ancillary rights in
perpetuity. Anyway, what a race, champ!

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.920
I didn't see it,
but I heard you were great.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.120
Thanks, Harv.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.880
Listen, they're giving you 20 tickets
for the tiebreaker thing in Cali.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.640
I'll pass 'em on to your friends.
Shoot me the names.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.840
- You let Harv rock it for you, baby.
- Right. Friends.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.840
Yes, there's...

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.400
OK, I get it, Mr. Popular.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.600
So many you can't even narrow it down.
Hey, when you get to town,

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.800
you better make time
for your best friend!

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.040
Break bread
with your mishpocheh here!

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.200
That'd be great!
We should totally...

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:30.040
OK, I gotta jump, kid.
Let me know how it goes. I'm out.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.120
- [dial tone hums]
- [sighing]

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.200
- [melodic beeping]
- [wheels squeaking]

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.360
[Lightning] What? A minivan?

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.120
Come on, you're in the slow lane.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.520
This is Lightning McQueen
you're hauling here.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.120
Just stopping off
for a quick breather, kid.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.640
- Old Mack needs a rest.
- Absolutely not.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.440
We're driving all night till we
get to California. We agreed to it.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.720
All night? May I remind you
federal DOT regs state...

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.840
Come on, I need to get there
before Chick and hang with Dinoco.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.000
[Mack groans]
All those sleeping trucks.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.800
Hey, kid,
I don't know if I can make it.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.320
Oh, sure you can, Mack.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.720
Look, it'll be easy.
I'll stay up with you.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.640
- All night?
- All night long.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.640
[snoring]

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.800
[engines slowing]

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.000
[snoring, gasping, blubbering]

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.080
[grunting]

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.080
[snoring] Uh!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:33.600
[blubbering]

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.320
- [rap music]
- [engines revving]

